%I A401045 #38 Oct 26 2026 09:53:44
%S A401045 4,10,110,220,250,320,410,550,640,740,880,970,1190,1270,1370,1900,
%T A401045 1960,1970,2030,2060,2090,2510,2720,3680,3850,3910,4100,4160,4510,
%U A401045 4820,4940,5260,5390,5710,6020,6470,6710,6730,6790,7150,7180,7450,7570,8060,8230,8810,9070
%N A401045 Sexy roots: Numbers k such that k^2 is the sum of a pair of sexy primes (p,p'=p+6).
%C A401045 k^2 = p + (p+6) with p and p+6 prime. Then k = 2m and p = 2m^2 - 3.
%C A401045 Theorem: all terms except a(1) = 4 are divisible by 10, so k^2 is divisible by 100 for every term except 16 = 5 + 11.
%C A401045 Proof: For p = 2 and p = 3, p+6 is composite. For p > 5, p ends in 1, 3, 7 or 9. If p ends in 9, then p+6 ends in 5 and is composite (it is > 5). If p ends in 1 or 3, then p + (p+6) ends in 8 or 2, which is never a square. So p ends in 7, p+6 ends in 3, and k^2 ends in 0. A square ending in 0 has a root ending in 0, so k^2 is divisible by 100. Only p = 5 remains: 5 + 11 = 16.
%C A401045 No sexy root is divisible by 3, which implies that sexy roots are disjoint from integer roots of sums of twin primes, as these are always divisible by 3.
%C A401045 It is not known whether this sequence is infinite. However, assuming the Bateman-Horn conjecture, infinitude would follow.
%H A401045 Peer Stelldinger, <a href="/A401045/b401045.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401045 a(n) = sqrt(2 * A086776(n) + 6). - _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 15 2026
%F A401045 a(n) = sqrt(A401046(n)). - _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 26 2026
%e A401045 a(1) = 4 because 5 + 11 = 16 = 4^2.
%e A401045 a(2) = 10 because 47 + 53 = 100 = 10^2.
%e A401045 a(3) = 110 because 6047 + 6053 = 12100 = 110^2.
%t A401045 Join[{4}, Select[Range[10, 10000, 10], PrimeQ[#] && PrimeQ[# + 6] & [#^2/2 - 3] &]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 26 2026 *)
%o A401045 (PARI) for(m = 2, 5000, {my(p = 2*m^2 - 3); if(isprime(p) && isprime(p + 6), print1(2*m,", "););})
%Y A401045 Cf. A023201, A046117, A104010, A086776, A152786, A401046.
%K A401045 nonn,new
%O A401045 1,1
%A A401045 _Peer Stelldinger_ and Anna Kathrin Holtwiesche, Oct 14 2026
